00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.201
No.


00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.361
No children.


00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.205
Do you want children?


00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.121
I do.


00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.884
Okay.


00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.961
Bradley?


00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.531
I just think we need
to be in a better place


00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.971
before we bring somebody else into it.


00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.247
Okay.


00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.803
Do you wanna say something, Lisa?


00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.209
I love him. It's just that I think
people change. Don't you agree?


00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.805
Yeah. They do.


00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.329
I often feel like we become
a lot of different people


00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.801
before we actually settle into who we are.


00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.890
Especially when we're young.


00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.571
We were 18.


00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.491
I'm not the same little girl
that was in love with him in high school.


00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.404
But I still love you.


00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.561
Tell me what
you want me to do. I promise I can change.


00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.087
Tell me, please.


00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.321
Just don't do that.


00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.488
I can't do this.


00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.450
I'm sorry.


00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.443
Bradley, don't. I'm sorry.


00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.166
I don't wanna hurt him. He deserves better.


00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.490
Better than you?


00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.641
Yeah.


00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.771
Why do you feel that way?


00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.771
He's a good guy.


00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.088
He's consistent and loving.


00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.003
